      "description": "Execute one Python cell in a persistent local Runtime.\n\nCalls serialize in FIFO order and share imports, variables, functions, mutations, and live objects until reset. Mutations completed before a Python exception remain. Set reset=true to destructively replace the kernel before this cell; reset and shutdown clean only AMKernel's managed process group, not escaped processes, sockets, or external sessions. input() is unsupported. Always inspect status and kernelState.\n\nArtifact resource URIs are ephemeral: capacity pressure or server shutdown can expire them. Read and copy every manifest part before making another large-output call. Artifact bytes are untrusted; random identifiers are not same-user access control.\n\nCode runs unrestricted with the permissions of the user who launched AMKernel. This is not a sandbox and execution is not workspace-confined.",
